WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.860
(GASPS)

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.020
Ahhhhhh!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.620
Ag-g-g-h!

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.900
-Have you lost your mind?
-But I thought...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.020
This chap needs a tow.
Hook him up.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.100
Sure thing.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.620
You rusty piece of junk!
Get your dirty hook off me!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.220
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.620
(SPEAKS FRENCH)

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.100
Electroshock! Are you kidding me?

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.060
This is her first field assignment. She
didn't know you were my informant.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.100
-Informant?
-A rookie, huh?

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.060
I never liked new car smell.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.900
Tomber was doing 20-to-life
in a Moroccan impound

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.900
the first time I saved him,
if I recall correctly.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.660
Speaking of recalls, you're getting up
there in mileage, aren't you?

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.740
All right, we get it. You both know
each other, you're both old.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.060
So, here you go, informant.
Inform us.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.980
Beuck!
That is the worst motor ever made.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:16.420
Wait. That oil filter.
Those wheel bearings.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.580
Do those parts look familiar, Tomber?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.660
They should. I sold them.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.260
-HOLLEY: To whom?
-No idea.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.740
He's my best customer, but he always
does his business over the phone.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.260
I was always wondering
why he needs so many parts.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.100
Now I know.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.340
A lemon needs parts.
Ain't nothin' truer than that.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.460
-Lemon?
-Yeah. Cars that don't ever work right.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.620
Lemons is a tow truck's
bread and butter.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.580
Like 'em Gremlins and Pacers
we run into at the party

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.220
and the race and the airport.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.340
Pull up the pictures
from the oil platform.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.820
I want to know what other type of cars
were out there.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.620
Right. Let's see.
There were Hugos and Trunkovs.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.460
Are these cars considered lemons?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.460
Is the Popemobile Catholic?

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.500
Everyone involved in this plot
is one of history's biggest loser cars.

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.660
And they're all taking their orders
from the car behind this engine.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.660
-Ah. This explains it.
-What, Tomber?

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:09.300
Gremlin, Pacer, Hugo
and Trunkov never get together,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.020
but they are having a secret meeting
in two days.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.260
-Where's this meeting taking place?
-Porto Corsa, Italy.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.020
That's where the next race is!

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.820
There's a good chance
our mystery engine will be there, too.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.900
Your chances are more than good.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.580
I just sent him a new clutch assembly
yesterday. To Porto Corsa.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.220
Contact Stevenson
and have him meet us at Gare de Lyon.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.740
Good work.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.500
MATER: That three-wheeled feller
had to be right about a big meetin'.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.020
You never see this many lemons
in one town.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.500
'Less there's a swap meet.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.380
How'd you get all them pictures?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.140
I reprogrammed Porto Corsa's red light
cameras to do recognition scans.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.260
Wow. Not only is you the purtiest car
I ever met, but you're the smartest, too.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.260
Thank you...I think.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.900
MATER: That's a familiar sight.
A Hugo being towed.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.780
But he looks absolutely perfect!

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.940
Of course! They must be the heads
of the lemon families.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.940
Makes sense. If I was rich
and broke down every day,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.380
I'd hire me to tow me
around all the time, too!

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.380
We've got to infiltrate that meeting
to find out who's behind all this.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.900
-Hang on a minute. Hold still.
-Ow!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.220
Ah-ha. Good job, Miss Shiftwell.

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.580
Thank you, Finn.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.540
Boy, I sure wish my friends
could see me now.

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.380
LUIGI: Guido,
your eyes do not deceive you.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.540
We are in Italy. We are home.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.820
Hey, Luigi.
Which way to the hotel, man?

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:50.140
What? No friend of mine
will stay in a hotel in-a my village.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:54.020
You will stay with my...
Uncle Topolino-o-o-o!

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.900
Luigi! Guido! (SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.100
How do they do it?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.460
These are the same ingredients
as back home, but it tastes so good.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.420
-It's organic, man.
-Treehugger.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.260
TOPOLINO: Hey, race car.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.340
You look so down, so low.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.340
Is like you have flat tires.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.420
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.660
She said you look like you are starving,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.180
that she's gonna make you a big meal
and fatten you up.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.500
Oh, no.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.580
Mama Topolino, please,
you don't need to make a fuss.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.780
Capisco. I understand.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.700
Is a problem, yes,
between you and a friend?

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.300
How did you know that?

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.540
A wise car hears one word
and understands two.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.140
That, and Luigi told me.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.380
While Mama cooks,
come and take a stroll with me.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.860
I brought my friend Mater along
on the trip

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.180
and I told him he needed
to act different,

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.780
that we weren't in Radiator Springs.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.940
This Mater is a close friend?

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.100
He's my best friend.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.660
Then why would you ask him to be
someone else?

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.020
What did I do?

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.020
I said some things during our fight.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.180
You know, back when Guido and Luigi
used to work for me,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.140
they would fight over everything.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:25.980
They fight over what Ferrari
was the best Ferrari,

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.940
which one of them looked
more like a Ferrari.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.460
There were even
some non-Ferrari fights.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.020
So I tell them, "Va bene, it's OK to fight.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.340
"Everybody fights now and then,
especially best friends.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.020
"But you got to make up fast.

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.660
"No fight more important
than friendship."

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:53.580
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:58.020
-What does that mean?
-Whoever find a friend, find a treasure.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:00.140
Now, mangia. Eat!

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.180
(THEY ARGUE IN ITALIAN)

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.860
Finn, one hour to Porto Corsa.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.740
Thank you, Stevenson.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.180
-That should just about do it.
-Perfect.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.860
So, Mater, it's voice-activated.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.820
But everything's voice-activated
these days.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.220
What? I thought you was supposed
to be makin' me a disguise.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.060
COMPUTER: Voice recognized.
Disguise program initiated.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.780
Cool!

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.860
Computer, make me a German truck.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.060
-Request acknowledged.
-Check it out! I'm wearing Materhosen.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:38.260
Make me a monster truck!

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.260
-Request acknowledged.
-What the...?

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.660
I vant to siphon your gas!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.780
-Now make me a taco truck!
-Request acknowledged.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.820
(HORN PLAYS LA CUCARACHA)

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.340
-A funny car!
-Request acknowledged.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:55.660
The idea is to keep a low profile, Mater.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.060
So I just go in, pretend to be this truck.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.940
-And leave the rest to us.
-Now, hold still.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.060
I have to do the final fitting
on your disguise.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.020
That's no good. Hm.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.580
Hey. What are you doin'?

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.500
The disguise won't calibrate effectively
without a smooth surface to graft onto.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.540
For a second there, I thought
you was tryin' to fix my dents.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.020
-Yes, I was.
-Then, no, thank you.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.940
I don't get them dents buffed,
pulled, filled or painted by nobody.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.500
-They way too valuable.
-Your dents are valuable? Really?

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:34.620
I come by each one of 'em with
my best friend, Lightning McQueen.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:38.300
I don't fix these.
I wanna remember these dents forever.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:43.740
So, you were being serious in Paris?
McQueen isn't just part of your cover.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.860
Friendships can be dangerous
in our line of work, Mater.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.980
But my line of work
is towin' and salvage.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:52.140
Right. And Miss Shiftwell's
is designing iPhone apps.

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.580
-No, I meant for real.
-It's OK. I'll work around the dent.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.140
-Oh...
-In the meantime...

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.980
..you look a little light on weapons.

